  "title": "Mutual selection at four places",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Mutual selection at four places: parity's count is polynomial; the clause and not-all-equal never fail; the not-exactly-two and twelve classes (FOUR-PLACE C) and ten value-preferring classes (B) build links and are NP-complete on 4-regular systems, so their failures are coNP-complete. Unless NP-complete problems are polynomial, a mutually selecting four-place knot would have to be one of five weak classes (13-17, two or three excluded states), none of which failed on any system examined (ticket C). Open: whether those five ever fail.",
